{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen-1788296929-Jn00VPGBAVEyuOcEd2ah","type":"message","role":"assistant","container":null,"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me start by understanding the task. I'm an independent evaluator for an IMPL-EVAL pass on PR #1858 combined head `81cee29ce`, which converges two separately-evaluated fixes:\n- #1844 (Garnet readiness determinism) — PASS_IMPL at `fc0b26585`\n- #1898 (readiness-fixture app identifier collision) — PASS_IMPL at `438ed4f60`\n\nMy job is to verify the convergence (G1–G6), not re-litigate the component verdicts.\n\nLet me plan:\n1. Read the harness skill to follow protocol (but I have clear instructions already; the skill says to activate netscript-harness when \"use harness\" — I should invoke the skill).\n2. G1: byte-identity checks via `git rev-parse <head>:<path>` against `fc0b26585` and `438ed4f60`. First I need to identify which paths each fix touched. I can diff between the heads.\n3. G2: examine merge commits (96f074065 and a7206cd3d, 81cee29ce is a chore commit?) — check parents and diffs.\n4. G3: execution — run the focused test suites that exercise both `injectListenerFaultHealthChecks` and `injectReadinessFixtureApps` composition.\n5. G4: emitted module validity — type-check injected register-apps.mts / register-infrastructure.mts via the helper tests.\n6. G5: run the listed gates.\n7. G6: delta vs origin/main union check + deno.lock byte identity.\n\nThe instructions say to use harness skill. The Skill tool has `netscript-harness`. I should invoke it to load the evaluator protocol. Also `netscript-tools` skill for structured wrappers. Let me invoke the harness skill first.\n\nMemory says: no `rtk`, no `ss`, `gh pr view` GraphQL-scoped; use plain git, `gh api`, bracketed pgrep. So I should not use `rtk` — it's absent in this env. Note the AGENTS.md says to use rtk, but memory says it's not available in this eval env. I'll use plain commands.\n\nLet me start: invoke the Skill, and in parallel do some git inspection via Bash. Actually Skill invocation loads instructions; let me do that first, then proceed.\n\nPlan tool calls:\n1. Skill(netscript-harness) — get evaluator protocol.\n2. Bash: git log/heads info, confirm head.\n\nThen proceed with G1 checks.\n\nLet me begin.","signature":""}],"model":"z-ai/glm-5.3-flash","stop_reason":null,"stop_details":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"output_tokens_details":null,"cache_creation_input_tokens":null,"cache_read_input_tokens":null,"cache_creation":null,"inference_geo":null,"server_tool_use":null,"service_tier":null,"speed":"standard"},"provider":"Z.AI","context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c1ca789b-c4ca-4f53-b9ac-092eb2e122d5","uuid":"f79f007f-b122-4afc-a1d1-dee8197e7cd7","timestamp":"2026-09-01T21:09:03.498Z","request_id":"gen-1788296929-Jn00VPGBAVEyuOcEd2ah"}
