{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen-1788296943-9CokTPUMxAztaCbAfeAd","type":"message","role":"assistant","container":null,"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm the IMPL-EVAL evaluator. Let me load the evaluator protocol and start the G1–G6 work. Let me first read the evaluator protocol file and check the run dir, then start git verification.\n\nPlan:\n1. Read `.llm/harness/evaluator/protocol.md` (IMPL-EVAL protocol).\n2. Confirm head = 81cee29ce in the worktree (git rev-parse HEAD).\n3. Identify the paths touched by #1844 (fc0b26585) and #1898 (438ed4f60) — diff each leaf against its merge-base with main, or better: diff fc0b26585 vs its parent, and 438ed4f60 vs its parent, to get the touched product paths.\n4. G1: `git rev-parse 81cee29ce:<path>` vs `git rev-parse fc0b26585:<path>` for each #1844 path; similarly vs 438ed4f60 for #1898 paths.\n5. G2: inspect merge commits 96f074065 (merge of #1898 branch into fix/garnet-readiness-timeout) and a7206cd3d (merge of origin/main). Check for conflict resolutions / non-union changes.\n6. G3: run the focused test suites (gates + aspire helpers tests) — these exercise composition.\n7. G4: verify emitted module validity — likely covered by the aspire helpers tests; possibly run a generation script. Check what tests exist.\n8. G5: run the scoped wrappers (run-deno-check for e2e, check:assets-barrel, quality:gate).\n9. G6: delta vs origin/main — `git diff --stat origin/main..81cee29ce` and check it's union of leaves + run artifacts; `git rev-parse origin/main:deno.lock` vs HEAD:deno.lock.\n10. Write verdict to `.llm/runs/fix-garnet-readiness-timeout--0.0.7/impl-eval-verdict-combined.md`.\n\nLet me start with parallel calls: read protocol.md, and run git commands.\n\nFirst batch:\n- Read protocol.md\n- Bash: git rev-parse HEAD, git log --oneline -8, git status --short\n- Bash: ls .llm/runs/fix-garnet-readiness-timeout--0.0.7/\n\nNote: memory says no rtk in this env — use plain git. Let me do that.","signature":""}],