{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen-1788298527-m6dQFNB1LMrhmPfJbjru","type":"message","role":"assistant","container":null,"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Important: `register-apps.mts` imports `type { InfrastructureContext } from './register-infrastructure.mts'` — so the two injected modules are **directly coupled**. This is the composition point the brief is asking about: register-apps.mts type-checks only if register-infrastructure.mts is present and exports InfrastructureContext. My type-check harness must have both files in the same helpers dir — and I'll check them together (deno check register-apps.mts pulls in register-infrastructure.mts via the import). That's a real joint type-check of BOTH injected modules.\n\nAlso register-apps imports (slot3) from compat: the value imports list at template lines 7-11 — let me see lines 7-12 of the template... The existing fixture test stubbed: buildOtelEnvVars, buildViteEnvVarName, resolveWorkspacePath, withCacheReference (+ NetScriptConfig type). Good.\n\nNow write the script. Structure:\n\n```ts\n#!/usr/bin/env -S deno run --allow-read --allow-write --allow-run\n// IMPL-EVAL G3/G4 composition proof — scratch, not product code.\nimport { generateRegisterApps } from '../../packages/cli/src/kernel/templates/aspire/helpers/register/generate-register-apps.ts';\nimport { generateRegisterInfrastructure } from '../../packages/cli/src/kernel/templates/aspire/helpers/register/generate-register-infrastructure.ts';\nimport {\n  injectListenerFaultHealthChecks,\n  injectReadinessFixtureApps,\n  TEST_ONLY_GARNET_HEALTH_KEY,\n  TEST_ONLY_POSTGRES_HEALTH_KEY,\n} from '../../packages/cli/e2e/src/application/gates/scaffold/runtime/prepare-readiness-fixture.ts';\nimport { DATABASE } from '../../packages/cli/e2e/src/domain/extension-axes.ts';\n```\n\nWait, script at `.llm/tmp/g3-composition-proof.mts`: `.llm/tmp` → up one is `.llm` → up two is worktree root. So `'../../packages/cli/...'` — from `.llm/tmp/x.mts`, `..` = `.llm`, `../..` = root. ✓.\n\nAssertion helpers: assert(cond, msg), counts.\n\nThen:\n\n```ts\n// 1. Real generator output — D-101 Postgres + Garnet Auto\nconst infraSource = generateRegisterInfrastructure({\n  databases: { postgres: { Enabled: true, Engine: 'Postgres', Mode: 'Container', Persistent: false } },\n  caches: { garnet: { Enabled: true, Engine: 'Garnet', Mode: 'Auto' } },\n  primaryDatabase: 'postgres',\n  primaryCache: 'garnet',\n});\nconst appsSource = generateRegisterApps({\n  apps: { app: { Enabled: true, Runtime: 'deno', Type: 'task', Workdir: 'apps/app', TaskName: 'start', WatchMode: false, RequiresKv: false } },\n  version: 'e2e',\n  denoDefaults: { Permissions: [], WatchMode: false },\n});\n\n// 2. Composition exactly as prepareReadinessFixture performs it\nconst injectedInfra = injectListenerFaultHealthChecks(infraSource, DATABASE.POSTGRES);\nconst injectedApps = injectReadinessFixtureApps(appsSource);\n```\n\nNote: prepareReadinessFixture injects apps BEFORE infra (order doesn't matter across files).\n\nAssertions A (infra):\n- pre: `healthLineCount(infraSource, '\"garnet_resp\"')` === 2 (Auto arms); `'\"postgres_listener\"'` === 1.\n- injected: TEST_ONLY_GARNET count === 2 (addHealthCheck lines), and `await cache_0.withHealthCheck('test_only_garnet_resp')` count === 2.\n- TEST_ONLY_POSTGRES addHealthCheck count === 1.\n- Per-arm placement: find real garnet attachment line indices; the line after each must be the test-only addHealthCheck; the two real attachments must be separated by the `} else {` boundary (one in container arm, one in executable arm). Also assert each arm contains EXACTLY ONE test-only registration: count TEST_ONLY_GARNET registrations between arm boundaries.\n- Real attachments preserved.\n\nAssertions B (apps):\n- no duplicate const bindings in injectedApps.\n- real binding intact: `const app_0_workdir` present without prefix — assert line `  const app_0_workdir = ...` exists.\n- fixture bindings: `const readiness_fixture_app_0