here generatedConfigPath = `${generatedRoot}/deno.json`. Same shape as mine.\n\nSo why TS2305?! Let me actually reproduce minimally — maybe the problem is that my stub was written as a .mts file but contains `export enum` re-declared... no.\n\nHmm — OR the write order: I write register-infrastructure.mts, _aspire-compat.mts, aspire.mts, deno.json — all before the loop. ✓\n\nWait wait. Look at my stub again — I declared `function ASPIRE_MODULE_STUB(): string {` AFTER the try/finally. Function declarations hoist... **in the same scope**. Is the function declaration hoisted when the module uses top-level await? Yes, hoisting is unaffected.\n\nHmm, but actually — there's a subtle Deno behavior: `deno run` type-checks the SCRIPT first; the script ran and produced output, so my script itself type-checked fine... \n\nLet me just reproduce the exact failing check in isolation to see the file content that deno sees. I'll recreate the temp workspace manually and keep it (no cleanup) to inspect.","signature":""}],"model":"z-ai/glm-5.3-flash","stop_reason":null,"stop_details":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"output_tokens_details":null,"cache_creation_input_tokens":null,"cache_read_input_tokens":null,"cache_creation":null,"inference_geo":null,"server_tool_use":null,"service_tier":null,"speed":"standard"},"provider":"Parasail","context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c1ca789b-c4ca-4f53-b9ac-092eb2e122d5","uuid":"1a52eb5b-81a3-4dbd-9288-ff6fe1396b01","timestamp":"2026-09-01T21:48:35.616Z","request_id":"gen-1788299294-demktCSTUjakBEypszu6"}
