{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen-1788299336-3uHLLniKU1MgN8nrlRcT","type":"message","role":"assistant","container":null,"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now the errors are real type-model mismatches in MY STUB, not the injected modules:\n\n1. `AspireResource` derives from `Parameters<ReturnType<DAB['addExecutable']>['waitFor']>[0]`. My addExecutable returns `PromiseLike<ExecutableResource> & ExecutableResource` — the `waitFor` on that intersection comes from ExecutableResource.waitFor(resource: AspireResourceBase) → param = AspireResourceBase. But the error says \"not assignable to type 'string'\" — meaning AspireResource resolved to `string`?! Because `PromiseLike<ExecutableResource> & ExecutableResource` — `waitFor` is ambiguous across the intersection: PromiseLike has no waitFor; ExecutableResource.waitFor(resource: AspireResourceBase). Hmm, \"Type 'PostgresServerResource' is not assignable to type 'string'\" — so Parameters<...> gave `string`?? That means waitFor's first param resolved to `string`... Intersection weirdness? Actually `Parameters<...>` on an intersection method — if `waitFor` resolves to the LAST overload or something odd... Whatever — the clean fix: make `waitFor`'s parameter a permissive type so derived AspireResource accepts all resources: `waitFor(resource: AspireResourceBase | string): ...`? Hmm.\n\n   Better approach: model the real SDK more faithfully — the real aspire.mts has a single resource type family. Actually, the REAL SDK: `builder.addExecutable` returns `ExecutableResourcePromise` etc. But since the template derives `AspireResource = Parameters<ReturnType<DAB['addExecutable']>['waitFor']>[0] & Parameters<...['withEnvironment']>[1]` — an intersection of the two parameter types. With my stub: waitFor param = AspireResourceBase, withEnvironment param = string → intersection `AspireResourceBase & string`. Hence \"not assignable to type 'string'\"... wait no, the error says PostgresServerResource is not assignable to `AspireResource` whose apparent type is... `AspireResourceBase & string`. Assigning PostgresServerResource to that fails on the string part. Yes! `withEnvironment(key: string, value: string)` — Parameters<...['withEnvironment']>[1] = string. So AspireResource = AspireResourceBase & string.\n\n   Fix: make `withEnvironment`'s second parameter the resource-ish type: in the real SDK, `withEnvironment(key, value)` where value: string | ResourceBuilder... The template's intersection expects the resource type to flow from BOTH. To make the stub faithful enough: type `withEnvironment(key: string, value: string | AspireResourceBase)`. Then Parameters[1] = string | AspireResourceBase → intersection with AspireResourceBase = AspireResourceBase. Then PostgresServerResource extends AspireResourceBase → assignable. \n\n2. `CacheResource = AspireResource | CacheContainerResource` where CacheContainerResource = Awaited<ReturnType<DAB['addContainer']>> = ContainerResource (my `PromiseLike<ContainerResource> & ContainerResource` awaited = ContainerResource). Error: ExecutableResource (from the Auto executable branch: `cache_0` = await builder.addExecutable...) not assignable to ContainerResource (missing withBindMount, withContainerRuntimeArgs). Because in the else-branch, `cache_0` is an ExecutableResource, and `caches.set(\"garnet\", cache_0)` — caches: Map<string, CacheResource> = Map<string, AspireResource | CacheContainerResource>. If AspireResource resolves properly to AspireResourceBase (per fix 1), ExecutableResource extends AspireResourceBase → assignable. So fix 1 resolves error 2 as well.\n\nSo single fix: `withEnvironment(key: string, value: string | AspireResourceBase)` on the base. But careful — the app module does `for (const [key, value] of Object.entries(app_0_otel)) { await app_0.withEnvironment(key, value); }` — value is string → fine with the union.\n\nAlso make sure addContainer's `withEnvironment` in container chains: `.withEnvironment('DENO_KV_ACCESS_TOKEN', cache_0_token)` — string ✓.\n\nOne more check — `AspireResource = & Parameters<...waitFor...>[0] & Parameters<...withEnvironment...>[1]`. With waitFor param AspireResourceBase and withEnvironment param `string | AspireResourceBase`: intersection = AspireResourceBase & (string | AspireResourceBase) = AspireResourceBase. ✓ Then Map<string, AspireResource> accepts PostgresServerResource. ✓ And AspireResource | CacheContainerResource accepts ExecutableResource. ✓\n\nAlso the header comment in my probe run: the injected register-infrastructure type-check got PAST all my injected lines (the errors are at generator-emitted lines 66/103 about resource maps, not about my injected test-only lines — my injected `builder.addHealthCheck('test_only_garnet_resp', createRespPingCheck(...))` produced NO error → the injected code type-checks against addHealthCheck(key, () => HealthCheckResult|Promise<...>) ✓ and createRespPingCheck returns () => Promise<HealthCheckResult> ✓ — the compat's HealthCheckResult comes from my stub too, consistent).\n\nLet me apply the stub fix.","signature":""}],"model":"z-ai/glm-5.3-flash","stop_reason":null,"stop_details":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"output_tokens_details":null,"cache_creation_input_tokens":null,"cache_read_input_tokens":null,"cache_creation":null,"inference_geo":null,"server_tool_use":null,"service_tier":null,"speed":"standard"},"provider":"Parasail","context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c1ca789b-c4ca-4f53-b9ac-092eb2e122d5","uuid":"6aa81de6-7c95-40b7-9ac5-c2a93b74ace8","timestamp":"2026-09-01T21:49:16.744Z","request_id":"gen-1788299336-3uHLLniKU1MgN8nrlRcT"}
