h B1.\n- N2 — this worktree contains no `packages/desktop-native`; the recorded root-lint REFUSAL baseline (exit 2, detached desktop-native fixture, missing catalog `zod`) is carried as stated. Focused wrappers were the verdict source, per the brief.\n- N3 — the combined run dir has no `context-pack.md`/`drift.md`; `worklog.md` (last 27 lines, commit `81cee29ce`) carries the convergence record including the circular-block table that motivated this head.\n- N4 — `fc0b26585`'s own merge carried combined-diff edits in `.llm/tools/agentic/*`; those are inside the already-judged #1844 leaf and later evolved by main commits — not convergence drift.\n\n## What I tried that failed to break it (negative results — all held)\n\n1. **Path-set forensics beyond the brief's list.** I rebuilt each leaf's product path set from its own non-merge commits (`git rev-list --first-parent --no-merges`, `git diff-tree`) rather than trusting the brief's counts, then diffed the *entire* product tree between `fc0b26585` and `81cee29ce` and attributed all 117 differing paths individually via `git log -- <path>`. Nothing unattributed; nothing touched by the convergence merges themselves.\n2. **Evil-merge hunt.** `git diff-tree --cc` on both merges (empty), plus union checks from both parents (`96f074065` vs `^1` = exact #1898 delta; `a7206cd3d` vs `^2` = exact #1844 delta). No merge smuggled a change.\n3. **Composition stress on real generator output.** 37-check execution proof against the real generators, including the hostile case a real app named `app` (which produces the same `app_0` binding index the fixture uses). The namespacing held; a deliberate negative control (stripping `readiness_fixture_`) reproduced the historical #1898 duplicate-binding collision, proving the existing test's collision assertion is load-bearing.\n4. **Module-validity stress.** Joint `deno check` of both injected modules against the real compat template with a faithful Aspire 13.5.3 stub (strict, `noImplicitAny`) —