byte-identical to `fc0b26585`; both #1898 paths byte-identical to `438ed4f60` (`git rev-parse <head>:<path>`). Every one of the 117 product paths differing between `fc0b26585` and the combined head attributes to a recorded `origin/main` commit (e.g. `159ede042`, `302409f0c`, `7d18ef104`, `9e3b8bcba`, `e938ecd31`) or to the two #1898 commits (`ad53835ee`, `38dab6c79`). Zero unattributed paths. |\n| G2 — merge soundness | **CONFIRMED** | `git diff-tree --cc` is **empty** for both merges `a7206cd3d` and `96f074065` — no manual conflict resolution. `96f074065` vs its branch-side parent = exactly the #1898 delta (16 run-artifact files + the 2 product paths). `a7206cd3d` vs its main-side parent = exactly the 9 #1844 paths. `81cee29ce` = 1 run-artifact worklog append. No third-party file modified. |\n| G3 — do the fixes interact | **REFUTED at runtime level** | Injection mechanics compose (37/37 execution checks, see G4), **but the hosted two-tier proof at this exact head failed both tiers** on `runtime.health.listener-unreachable`: sqlite tier FAILED 30929 ms, postgres tier FAILED 52033 ms (passed=53/57, each failing only this gate). Deterministic root cause below. |\n| G4 — emitted module validity | **CONFIRMED** | Independent composition proof (`.llm/tmp/g3-composition-proof.mts`, exit 0, 37/37): joint `deno check` of the injected `register-infrastructure.mts` and injected `register-apps.mts` (which imports `InfrastructureContext` from it — a true joint type-check) against the **real** `_aspire-compat.ts.template`; exactly one test-only `addHealthCheck` registration in each `Mode: 'Auto'` arm; test-only attachment directly follows each real attachment and binds the same resource; fixture bindings namespaced with the real `app_0` binding preserved; no duplicate const bindings. |\n| G5 — suites and gates | **CONFIRMED focused / REFUTED release class** | `run-deno-test` e2e gates: **121 passed / 0 failed, exit 0** (3.2 s). `run-deno-test` aspire helpers: **254 passed / 0 failed, exit 0** (7.8 s). `run-deno-check --root packages/cli/e2e --ext ts`: 190 files, 0 errors, exit 0. `deno task check:assets-barrel`: exit 0 (regenerated, `git diff --exit-code` clean across all 7 barrels). `deno task quality:gate`: exit 0 (advisory F-5/F-6 `export default` WARNs only). **Hosted `scaffold.runtime` (release class): FAILED both tiers.** Root e2e lint: recorded as **REFUSAL** per known baseline, never PASS/FAIL. |\n| G6 — ceiling and lock | **CONFIRMED** | Full delta vs `origin/main` (merge-base `159ede042`) = exactly the 11-path union (9 #1844 ∪ 2 #1898) plus `.llm/runs/**` artifacts; `deno.lock` blob `23cb256ba9f04168dda01dddfb493b480fb621f7` byte-identical to `origin/main:deno.lock`. |\n\n## Blocking finding (the one that decides the verdict)\n\n### B1 — `runtime.health.listener-unreachable` fails deterministically on the Garnet arm at the combined head\n\nHosted run `33559334374` at exactly `81cee29ce`, terminal failure on **both** tiers, identical signature:\n\n```\nscaffold-runtime-sqlite (aspire + sqlite + garnet)   FAILED 30929ms\nscaffold-runtime (aspire + docker + postgres)        FAILED 52033ms\n  error: garnet healthReports.test_only_garnet_resp missed its 30s transition;\n         last=Unhealthy: RESP listener unhealthy: ECONNREFUSED at localhost:18999\n         after 1 ms; received=\"\"\n    at pollReport (listener-unreachable-fixture.ts:266)\n  FAILED GATE: runtime.health.listener-unreachable\n```\n\nRoot cause — a description-wording drift **between the two #1844 sides and main's D-101 gate**:\n\n| Side | Content |\n| --- | --- |\n| Old probe (`origin/main` `_aspire-compat.ts.template` line 270) | `description: \\`RESP listener unreachable: ${code}\\`` |\n| New probe (this head, #1844 rewrite, line 321) | `` `RESP listener unhealthy: ${code} at ${host}:${port} after ${data.elapsedMs} ms; received=\"${data.received}\"` `` |\n| Gate regex (`listener-unreachable-fixture.ts:216`, **byte-identical to `origin/main`**, outside both fixes' path sets) | `/RESP listener unreachable: (?:ECONNREFUSED|ETIMEDOUT)/` |\n\nAfter the fixture commands the Garnet listener closed, the health report is correctly `Unhealthy` (the #1844 named-health instrumentation and the #1898 controller both **work** — `runtime.wait.garnet` PASSED in 1106 ms sqlite / fast postgres, and the close transition is observed) — but the description never satisfies the stale regex, so `pollReport` burns its full 30 s deadline and throws. The Postgres arm passes because the TCP probe's wording (`${kind} listener unreachable`, kind `tcp`) was left unchanged. No test anywhere pairs `expectedUnhealthyDescription` with the probe's actual output, and no remaining reference to `RESP listener unreachable` exists outside the stale regex — the pairing was never under test.\n\nWhy each component verdict still carries: at `438ed4f60` the gate ran against the **old** probe wording and passed (30558 ms hosted). At `fc0b26585` the gate could not pass for a different reason (the #1898 collision left the controller unregistered — the documented circular block), so the wording drift was invisible. Only the converged head brings both changes together, and the convergence was created precisely to earn this runtime proof. It did not earn it.\n\nClassification: **blocking**. `scaffold.runtime` is a release-class gate and it is red at the judged head on both tiers with a deterministic, code-caused trigger — not a flake (both tiers, exact 30 s deadline timeouts, word-level drift reproducible by inspection from the sources).\n\nNext action for the implementing lane: align the D-101 gate with the new RESP description contract (accept the richer `RESP listener unhealthy: <code> at host:port after N ms; received=\"…\"` form for ECONNREFUSED/ETIMEDOUT), and add the missing pairing test asserting `createRespPingCheck`'s ECONNREFUSED/ETIMEDOUT descriptions against `expectedUnhealthyDescription`. Note that `origin/fix/garnet-readiness-timeout` has since advanced to `28e2cd6a4` with two commits (`7aae355ed`, `28e2cd6a4`) touching exactly this file — outside this verdict's mandate; the next eval pass must judge that head.\n\n## Non-blocking observations\n\n- N1 — `run 33559274152` (`e2e-cli`, push) was cancelled/superseded; `33559274116` (`ci`) also failed at this head. Redundant with B1.\n- N2 — this worktree contains no `packages/desktop-native`; the recorded root-lint REFUSAL baseline (exit 2, detached desktop-native fixture, missing catalog `zod`) is carried as stated. Focused wrappers were the verdict source, per the brief.\n- N3 — the combined run dir has no `context-pack.md`/`drift.md`; `worklog.md` (last 27 lines, commit `81cee29ce`) carries the convergence record including the circular-block table that motivated this head.\n- N4 — `fc0b26585`'s own merge carried combined-diff edits in `.llm/tools/agentic/*`; those are inside the already-judged #1844 leaf and later evolved by main commits — not convergence drift.\n\n## What I tried that failed to break it (negative results — all held)\n\n1. **Path-set forensics beyond the brief's list.** I rebuilt each leaf's product path set from its own non-merge commits (`git rev-list --first-parent --no-merges`, `git diff-tree`) rather than trusting the brief's counts, then diffed the *entire* product tree between `fc0b26585` and `81cee29ce` and attributed all 117 differing paths individually via `git log -- <path>`. Nothing unattributed; nothing touched by the convergence merges themselves.\n2. **Evil-merge hunt.** `git diff-tree --cc` on both merges (empty), plus union checks from both parents (`96f074065` vs `^1` = exact #1898 delta; `a7206cd3d` vs `^2` = exact #1844 delta). No merge smuggled a change.\n3. **Composition stress on real generator output.** 37-check execution proof against the real generators, including the hostile case a real app named `app` (which produces the same `app_0` binding index the fixture uses). The namespacing held; a deliberate negative control (stripping `readiness_fixture_`) reproduced the historical #1898 duplicate-binding collision, proving the existing test's collision assertion is load-bearing.\n4. **Module-validity stress.** Joint `deno check` of both injected modules against the real compat template with a faithful Aspire 13.5.3 stub (strict, `noImplicitAny`) — no test in the repo had ever type-checked the injected `register-infrastructure.mts`; it type-checks.\n5. **Double-injection / fail-closed checks.** Re-running `injectListenerFaultHealthChecks` on its own output throws (`test-only listener health checks were already registered`); the Garnet-only path registers no Postgres test key; missing markers fail closed. All held.\n6. **Re-run / newer-evidence hunt.** All 7 workflow runs at this sha enumerated — no green re-run exists for `e2e-cli` at `81cee29ce`.\n7. Two earlier FAILs in my own harness were mine, not the code's: an arm-window slicing bug that excluded post-attachment lines, a hardcoded `cache_0` binding (sqlite config uses `cache_1`), passing the stub function instead of calling it (so the module serialized without exports), and an `AspireResource` intersection-derivation mismatch in the stub (`withEnvironment` value widened to `string | AspireResourceBase`). All corrected; the final run is 37/37 exit 0.\n\n## Required inputs status\n\nRead and used: run `plan.md`, `research.md`, `worklog.md` (convergence section), component verdicts in the run dirs, merge/commit trail, gate docs, `listener-unreachable-fixture.ts` + `listener-readiness-gates.ts` + `prepare-readiness-fixture.ts` + `generate-register-infrastructure.ts` + compat template at this head, hosted run logs and the sqlite report artifact. Not present in this run dir: `context-pack.md`, `drift.md` (noted in N3). Verdict path honors the brief: this file, Markdown, no transcript.\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false}}
