{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a06c59e8b7f7c420","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tname: eval-env-tool-gaps\n3\tdescription: \"In the agentic evaluator runtime, `rtk` is not installed and `gh pr view` fails on GraphQL scopes — use plain commands and `gh api repos/...`\"\n4\tmetadata: \n5\t  node_type: memory\n6\t  type: project\n7\t  originSessionId: 578bc6cf-ec9d-4aea-ae50-b5b4f29f7a32\n8\t  modified: 2026-09-01T18:07:46.804Z\n9\t---\n10\t\n11\tIn the `.config/netscript-agentic` evaluator runtime (worktree-based IMPL-EVAL/PLAN-EVAL sessions),\n12\tAGENTS.md recommends prefixing read-heavy commands with `rtk`, but `rtk` is not installed there\n13\t(`bash: command not found: rtk`) — run plain `git`/`grep` instead. Also `gh pr view` fails with a\n14\tGraphQL `read:org` scope error; the REST API works: `gh api repos/rickylabs/netscript/pulls/<n>`.\n15\t`ss` is also absent; use `pgrep -f '[p]attern'` (bracket trick — `pkill -f` otherwise kills the\n16\tsession's own shell) and fallback port checks.\n17\t\n18\t**Why:** These gaps cost several failed commands at the start of an evaluator session (2026-09-01,\n19\tPR #1883 eval) before being worked around.\n20\t\n21\t**How to apply:** In fresh evaluator sessions on this runtime, skip `rtk`/`ss`/`gh pr view` attempts\n22\tand go straight to plain git, `gh api`, and pgrep-based process checks.\n23\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c1ca789b-c4ca-4f53-b9ac-092eb2e122d5","uuid":"d79c6532-6b70-4c25-9ec2-27164d88a561","timestamp":"2026-09-01T21:55:26.934Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/agent/.config/netscript-agentic/runtime/claude-openrouter/projects/-home-agent-projects-netscript-repo/memory/eval-env-tool-gaps.md","content":"---\nname: eval-env-tool-gaps\ndescription: \"In the agentic evaluator runtime, `rtk` is not installed and `gh pr view` fails on GraphQL scopes — use plain commands and `gh api repos/...`\"\nmetadata: \n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: 578bc6cf-ec9d-4aea-ae50-b5b4f29f7a32\n  modified: 2026-09-01T18:07:46.804Z\n---\n\nIn the `.config/netscript-agentic` evaluator runtime (worktree-based IMPL-EVAL/PLAN-EVAL sessions),\nAGENTS.md recommends prefixing read-heavy commands with `rtk`, but `rtk` is not installed there\n(`bash: command not found: rtk`) — run plain `git`/`grep` instead. Also `gh pr view` fails with a\nGraphQL `read:org` scope error; the REST API works: `gh api repos/rickylabs/netscript/pulls/<n>`.\n`ss` is also absent; use `pgrep -f '[p]attern'` (bracket trick — `pkill -f` otherwise kills the\nsession's own shell) and fallback port checks.\n\n**Why:** These gaps cost several failed commands at the start of an evaluator session (2026-09-01,\nPR #1883 eval) before being worked around.\n\n**How to apply:** In fresh evaluator sessions on this runtime, skip `rtk`/`ss`/`gh pr view` attempts\nand go straight to plain git, `gh api`, and pgrep-based process checks.\n","numLines":23,"startLine":1,"totalLines":23}}}
