{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen-1788299736-9KskQISlxSGiFyxRyNJn","type":"message","role":"assistant","container":null,"content":[{"type":"text","text":"**FAIL_IMPL** — verdict written to `.llm/runs/fix-garnet-readiness-timeout--0.0.7/impl-eval-verdict-combined.md`, committed as `79e3f84ce` (verdict file only).\n\n## The decision\n\nThe convergence **merge** is sound, but the combined head fails the runtime proof it was created to earn. Hosted run `33559334374` at exactly `81cee29ce` is terminal **failure on both tiers**, with a deterministic root cause I confirmed from the sources:\n\n| Side | Content |\n| --- | --- |\n| `origin/main` probe | `RESP listener unreachable: ${code}` |\n| #1844 probe (this head, line 321) | `RESP listener unhealthy: ${code} at host:port after N ms; received=\"…\"` |\n| D-101 gate regex (`listener-unreachable-fixture.ts:216`, byte-identical to main) | `/RESP listener unreachable: (?:ECONNREFUSED\\|ETIMEDOUT)/` |\n\nAfter the fixture closes the Garnet listener, the report is correctly `Unhealthy` — but the description never satisfies the stale regex, so `pollReport` burns its full 30 s deadline on **both** tiers (sqlite FAILED 30929 ms, postgres FAILED 52033 ms, each losing only this one gate). The Postgres arm passes only because the TCP probe's wording was left unchanged. Each component verdict still carries: at `438ed4f60` the gate ran against the old wording and passed; at `fc0b26585` the gate couldn't pass at all (the documented circular block), so the drift was invisible. Only the converged head joins them.\n\n## What held (tried hard to break it)\n\n- **G1** — all 11 product paths byte-identical to their leaves; all 117 product-path differences vs `fc0b26585` attributed individually to recorded `origin/main` commits or the two #1898 commits. Zero unattributed.\n- **G2** — both merges have **empty** `--cc` combined diffs; union checks from both parents are exact; `81cee29ce` touches one run-artifact worklog.\n- **G4** — my own 37-check composition proof (exit 0): joint `deno check` of both injected modules against the **real** compat template, exactly one test-only registration per `Mode: 'Auto'` arm, fixture bindings collision-free with a real `app` present, and a negative control that reproduces the #1898 collision when the prefix is stripped.\n- **G5** — 121/121 e2e gates, 254/254 aspire helpers, scoped check 190 files/0 errors, `check:assets-barrel` clean, `quality:gate` exit 0. `runtime.wait.garnet` PASSED in 1106 ms hosted — the #1844 Garnet repair itself works.\n- **G6** — delta vs `origin/main` is exactly the 11-path union plus run artifacts; `deno.lock` byte-identical.\n\n## Next action\n\nOne-line contract fix: align the gate regex with the new RESP description (plus the missing pairing test no test currently covers). Note `origin/fix/garnet-readiness-timeout` has already advanced to `28e2cd6a4` with two commits touching exactly this file — outside my mandate; the next eval pass must judge that head.\n\nThree early FAILs in my own harness were mine (arm-window slicing, hardcoded `cache_0`, an uncalled stub function, a stub type-derivation mismatch) — documented in the verdict's negative-results section. Two tool lessons (`gh api` job logs need `--allow-escape-sequences`; runs-by-sha query) are saved to memory.","citations":[]}],"model":"z-ai/glm-5.3-flash","stop_reason":null,"stop_details":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"output_tokens_details":null,"cache_creation_input_tokens":null,"cache_read_input_tokens":null,"cache_creation":null,"inference_geo":null,"server_tool_use":null,"service_tier":null,"speed":"standard"},"provider":"Parasail","context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c1ca789b-c4ca-4f53-b9ac-092eb2e122d5","uuid":"712b4d28-1ad6-406f-b523-08b6212500f7","timestamp":"2026-09-01T21:55:46.069Z","request_id":"gen-1788299736-9KskQISlxSGiFyxRyNJn"}
